  "result": "All 5 tests pass, including both new ones in tests/test_t2.py and the existing tests in tests/test_t1.py.\n\n**What I changed** (all in `netgraph/graph.py`, appended to the existing adjacency-set `Graph` class):\n\n- **`remove_edge(u, v) -> bool`** validates both ids, returns False if the edge is absent, otherwise discards it from both neighbour sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns True. Self-loops work because the second discard is a no-op.\n- **`degree(u) -> int`** returns the size of the node's neighbour set. A self-loop is stored once as `u in adj[u]`, so it naturally counts once.\n- **`connected_components() -> list[list[int]]`** does an iterative depth-first search from each unseen node in increasing order. Each component is sorted before being appended. Since starts are visited in ascending order, components come out ordered by their smallest node without an extra sort.\n\nNo files under `tests/` were touched, and the code stays standard-library only. Nothing has been committed. The graph module and tests/test_t2.py remain untracked, as they were when I started.",
